#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""make-pack CAPRICORE_DIR [OUT_DIR] [--moods FILE] [--persona FILE] [--sleep FILE] [--v122 DIR] [--lachy DIR|auto] [--mochi DIR|auto]
          [--mochi-hair red|flat|original]
          [--upscale [--record-upscale]]

Build the Capri character pack from a CapriCore checkout (https://github.com/CapriChooms/CapriCore).
The artwork is third-party (see the pack's NOTICE.md): it is never committed to this repo; this
script assembles it on your machine.

PINNED: the checkout must be CapriCore v1.0.4 (bc93892). Every file copied is checked against
tools/capricore-v1.0.4.sha256 and make-pack refuses anything else (1.1.x retired and redrew most
of the frames her behaviour uses). One frame comes from v1.1.2 (bb0c2d7): pose-sleep, checked
against its own pinned sha256. It is read from the checkout's git objects if they have it, else
from --sleep FILE, else downloaded from GitHub at that commit.

Beside them, CapriCore v1.2.2 (828f272): her wave, the hanging and ledge cels and the no-jacket redraws
(her second outfit), each checked against tools/capricore-v1.2.2.sha256: from --v122 DIR (a v1.2.2
checkout), else the checkout's git objects, else downloaded from GitHub at that commit (cached).

OUT_DIR defaults to $XDG_DATA_HOME/synaps-avatar/packs/capri (~/.local/share/...).
--moods defaults to packs/capri/moods.json in this repo (the avatar's own behaviour file).
--persona defaults to packs/capri/persona.md in this repo: her session's system prompt (`[session] persona`).

Layout produced:
  sprites.json          <- assets/capri/sprites/v1/runtime-sprite-set.json
  capri-*.png           <- assets/capri/sprites/v1/*.png + assets/default/capri-headpat.png
  poses/poses.json      <- assets/capri/sprites/poses-v2/runtime-poses.json (+ PNG/*.png)
  poses/capri-sleep.png <- v1.1.2 assets/capri/sprites/poses-v2/PNG/capri-sleep.png
  intro/0[2-6]-*.png    <- assets/capri/intro-v1/PNG (+ runtime-intro.json); her bolt replaces 01,
                           and 07 is her neutral frame
  music/*.png           <- assets/default/capri-music-v1/*.png
  anim/capricore/       <- v1.2.2 assets/default/capri-wave.webp, hanging-cels/*.webp (anim.json: capricore)
  outfits/no-jacket/    <- v1.2.2 redraws + sprites.json (tools/capricore-outfit.json), her no-jacket look
  icon.png              <- assets/default/icon-source.png
  fonts/Exo2-*.ttf      <- static instances of assets/fonts/exo2/Exo2-Variable.ttf (fontTools), + OFL.txt
  NOTICE.md             <- docs/character-assets.md + one line naming the CapriCore versions
  moods.json            <- --moods
  persona.md            <- --persona

Optional desktop art (anim/; a pack without it still loads):
  --lachy DIR|auto   lachydotmcg/capri-desktop at 156ed18 (PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0): a checkout, or
                     `auto` to download the pinned files from GitHub at that commit (cached). Every file is
                     checked against tools/lachy-desktop-156ed18.sha256.
                     anim/lachy/sprites/*.png, capri.png, perch.png, cursor.png, emotes/<name>/ (unzipped),
                     LICENSE.md
  --mochi DIR|auto   mochiiwuff/capri-desktop at c011764, checked against tools/mochi-desktop-c011764.sha256.
                     anim/mochi/*.png|webp, LICENSE. Show frames, a fan cut-out and fan art; its code is
                     under PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0, and NOTICE.md quotes its README's "Credits and
                     rights" on the images. Downloaded onto this machine; the art files aren't in this repo.
  --mochi-hair MODE  her hair in the intro close-ups (anim/mochi/intro-*), which mochi drew black: `red`
                     (default: her avatar's red, shadow and starfield), `flat` (one red) or `original`.
                     tools/mochi_hair.py, deterministic, lossless WebP; anim.json pins the written bytes
                     (+ "hair" and the source's "sourceSha256"). Needs numpy and Pillow unless `original`.
  anim/anim.json     <- tools/desktop-art.json (our measured geometry) + the sha256 of every file copied
  NOTICE.md          + each source's Required Notice lines, licence URL and credits
  --upscale          + anim/lachy/x2/sprites/*.png: every strip x2 (tools/upscale_art.py, Real-ESRGAN
                     anime video model, CPU, needs torch); pixels checked against tools/lachy-x2.sha256.
                     --record-upscale writes that pin file instead (once, on the machine that sets it).
Then run `synaps-avatar --pack OUT_DIR --check` to verify it (sha256 of every frame)."""
import hashlib, json, os, shutil, subprocess, sys, urllib.request, zipfile
from pathlib import Path

